row(8, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'AND HE HUMBLED YOU AND LET YOU HUNGER AND FED YOU THE MANNA WHICH YOU DID NOT KNOW NOR DID YOUR FATHERS KNOW, TO MAKE YOU KNOW THAT NOT BY BREAD ALONE DOES MAN LIVE, BUT BY EVERYTHING THAT PROCEEDS FROM THE MOUTH OF THE LORD DOES MAN LIVE. {HP(8, 3, (("ויענך", "וירעבך", "ויאכלך", "את", "המן"), "and He humbled you and let you hunger and fed you the manna — THE CHAPTER\'S THREE NARRATIVE VERBS, all God\'s past acts in one verse (the morphology); \'the manna\' thirteen seats (computed)"), (("אשר", "לא", "ידעת", "ולא", "ידעון", "אבתיך"), "which you did not know nor did your fathers know — \'nor did your fathers know\' 8:3 and 8:16 alone; the paragogic nun on the perfect (computed)"), (("כי", "לא", "על", "הלחם", "לבדו", "יחיה", "האדם"), "that not by bread alone does man live — ONE seat; \'man shall live\' 8:3 and Ecclesiastes 11:8 (computed)"), (("כי", "על", "כל", "מוצא", "פי", "יהוה"), "but by everything that proceeds from the mouth of the LORD — ONE seat; \'the mouth of the LORD\' twenty-five Torah seats, the journeys\' formula, this the one where the mouth\'s issue is the food (computed)"))} → {AP(8, 3, (("ועניך", "ואכפנך", "ואוכלך", "ית", "מנא"), "and He humbled you and made you hungry and fed you the manna — each verb one seat (computed)"), (("לא", "על", "לחמא", "בלחודוהי", "מתקים", "אנשא"), "not by bread alone is man SUSTAINED — \'lives\' made \'is sustained\' (the sustaining verb 8:3 twice, 18:22, 19:15, 32:12 — computed)"), (("על", "כל", "אפקות", "מימרא", "דיי", "יתקים", "אנשא"), "by everything that PROCEEDS FROM THE WORD (MEMRA) OF THE LORD is man sustained — THE MEMRA: the mouth made the Word (\'the Memra of the LORD\' twenty-four seats over the book, 8:3 and 8:20 the chapter\'s two — computed)"))}. THE SHELF (48:10): \'bread\' the midrash, \'everything that proceeds\' the laws and the homilies. MATERIAL for the Memra and the three narrative verbs.')
row(8, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'YOUR GARMENT DID NOT WEAR OUT UPON YOU, AND YOUR FOOT DID NOT SWELL, THESE FORTY YEARS. {HP(8, 4, (("שמלתך", "לא", "בלתה", "מעליך"), "your garment did not wear out upon you — the singular garment (29:4 the plural clothes; Nehemiah 9:21 the kin); the wear-verb\'s Torah seats 8:4, 29:4 twice, Sarah\'s \'after I am worn\' (computed)"), (("ורגלך", "לא", "בצקה"), "and your foot did not swell — THE VERB\'S TWO SEATS IN THE BIBLE, 8:4 and Nehemiah 9:21 (computed)"), (("זה", "ארבעים", "שנה"), "these forty years — [40], the parser\'s second number verse (asserted)"))} → {AP(8, 4, (("כסותך", "לא", "אבליאת", "מנך"), "your covering did not wear out from you — the garment the covering-word (8:4, 22:12 — computed)"), (("ומסנך", "לא", "יחפו"), "AND YOUR SHOES DID NOT GO BARE — the foot made the SHOE: the Aramaic reads what covered the foot where the Hebrew reads the foot (the shoe-word 8:4, 29:4 — computed; 29:4\'s Hebrew has the sandal)"), (("דנן", "ארבעין", "שנין"), "these forty years"))}. THE KIN: 29:4 \'your clothes did not wear out upon you, and your sandal did not wear out upon your foot\' — the sandal there, the foot here, and Onkelos gives 8:4 the sandal of 29:4 (the diff). MATERIAL for the shoe.')
row(8, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL KNOW WITH YOUR HEART THAT AS A MAN DISCIPLINES HIS SON, THE LORD YOUR GOD DISCIPLINES YOU. {HP(8, 5, (("וידעת", "עם", "לבבך"), "and you shall know with your heart — \'with your heart\' 8:5 and 15:9 in the book (computed)"), (("כי", "כאשר", "ייסר", "איש", "את", "בנו"), "that as a man disciplines his son — ONE seat; \'as a man … his son\' 8:5 and 1:31 (the carrying) and 2 Kings 23:10 (Molech) (computed); the discipline-lemma eight Torah seats (computed)"), (("יהוה", "אלהיך", "מיסרך"), "the LORD your God disciplines you — the participle (the morphology)"))} → {AP(8, 5, (("ותדע", "עם", "לבך"), "and you shall know with your heart"), (("ארי", "כמא", "די", "מאלף", "גברא", "ית", "בריה"), "that as a man TEACHES his son — \'disciplines\' made \'TEACHES\', 4:1\'s teaching-word (the two seats — computed)"), (("יי", "אלהך", "מאלף", "לך"), "the LORD your God teaches you"))}. THE SHELF (32:10, 32:12, 32:15): the chastisement not as the deed; a covenant cut for chastisements as for the Land — 8:5 with 8:7. MATERIAL for \'teaches\' and the shelf\'s covenant of chastisements.')
row(8, 6, 'CONTEXT', f'AND YOU SHALL KEEP THE COMMANDMENTS OF THE LORD YOUR GOD, TO WALK IN HIS WAYS AND TO FEAR HIM. {HP(8, 6, (("ושמרת", "את", "מצות", "יהוה", "אלהיך"), "and you shall keep the commandments of the LORD your God — 28:9\'s clause (the diff, four tokens shared)"), (("ללכת", "בדרכיו", "וליראה", "אתו"), "to walk in His ways and to fear Him — \'to walk in His ways\' 8:6, 30:16, 1 Kings 2:3; \'and to fear Him\' ONE seat (computed)"))} → {AP(8, 6, (("למהך", "בארחן", "דתקנן", "קדמוהי", "ולמדחל", "יתיה"), "to walk in the ways that are RIGHT BEFORE HIM and to fear Him — the supplement at five seats (8:6, 19:9, 26:17, 28:9, 30:16 — computed)"))}. Terse: the charge between the way and the land.')
row(8, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD BRINGS YOU INTO A GOOD LAND, A LAND OF BROOKS OF WATER, OF SPRINGS AND DEEPS FLOWING IN THE VALLEY AND IN THE HILL. {HP(8, 7, (("כי", "יהוה", "אלהיך", "מביאך", "אל", "ארץ", "טובה"), "for the LORD your God brings you into a good land — \'a good land\' twelve seats, 8:7 and 8:10 among them; Exodus 3:8\'s \'to a good land\' the kin (three tokens shared) (computed)"), (("ארץ", "נחלי", "מים"), "a land of brooks of water — 8:7, 10:7 (Jotbah), Jeremiah 31:9 (computed)"), (("עינת", "ותהמת", "יצאים", "בבקעה", "ובהר"), "springs and deeps flowing in the valley and in the hill — \'springs and deeps\' ONE; \'deeps\' in the Torah 8:7 and the Song of the Sea (Exodus 15:5, 8); \'in the valley and in the hill\' ONE (11:11 \'a land of hills and valleys\') (computed)"))} → {AP(8, 7, (("ארי", "יי", "אלהך", "מעלך", "לארעא", "טבתא"), "for the LORD your God brings you into the good land"), (("ארעא", "נגדא", "נחלין", "דמיין"), "a land of FLOWING brooks of water — \'flowing\' supplied (one seat, computed)"), (("מבועי", "עינין", "ותהומין", "נפקין", "בבקען", "ובטורין"), "FOUNTAINS of springs and deeps going out in valleys and hills — \'fountains\' supplied (one seat); the plurals"))}. THE SHELF: 19:2 (Moses\' forty-year refrain), 32:12 and 32:15 (with 8:5), 39:4 (two of the twelve lands), 39:6 and 39:8 (the Land drinks from below too). MATERIAL for the Land\'s praise the shelf quotes most.')
row(8, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'A LAND OF WHEAT AND BARLEY AND VINE AND FIG AND POMEGRANATE, A LAND OF OLIVE OIL AND HONEY. {HP(8, 8, (("ארץ", "חטה", "ושערה", "וגפן", "ותאנה", "ורמון"), "a land of wheat and barley and vine and fig and pomegranate — the first \'land\' with five; THE ONE VERSE IN THE BIBLE HOLDING ALL SEVEN LEMMAS (three or more at five other seats — Numbers 20:5, Haggai 2:19, Joel 1:12, Habakkuk 3:17, Jeremiah 41:8) (computed on the lemmas)"), (("ארץ", "זית", "שמן", "ודבש"), "a land of olive oil and honey — the second \'land\' with two; ONE seat (2 Kings 18:32 the Rabshakeh\'s kin, \'a land of olive\' shared); HONEY WITHOUT MILK — \'milk\' absent from the chapter, \'flowing with milk and honey\' twenty seats elsewhere (computed); NO VERB, NO PERSON — the chapter\'s one verse with neither number (the morphology)"))} → {AP(8, 8, (("ארעא", "חטין", "וסערין", "וגופנין", "ותאנין", "ורמונין"), "a land of wheats and barleys and vines and figs and pomegranates — the seven species PLURAL, each token one seat (computed)"), (("ארעא", "דזיתהא", "עבדין", "משחא", "והיא", "עבדא", "דבש"), "a land WHOSE OLIVES MAKE OIL AND WHICH MAKES HONEY — the two supplements (the English\'s brackets \'yeilding oil\', \'producing\'), one seat each (computed)"))}. THE SHELF (297:4): the first-fruits from the seven kinds by which the Land is praised — this verse the list; (39:4) two of the twelve lands. MATERIAL for the seven and the honey.')
row(8, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'A LAND WHERE YOU SHALL EAT BREAD WITHOUT POVERTY, YOU SHALL NOT LACK ANYTHING IN IT; A LAND WHOSE STONES ARE IRON AND FROM WHOSE HILLS YOU SHALL HEW COPPER. {HP(8, 9, (("ארץ", "אשר", "לא", "במסכנת", "תאכל", "בה", "לחם"), "a land where not in poverty shall you eat bread in it — \'in poverty\' the lemma\'s ONE seat in the Bible (computed)"), (("לא", "תחסר", "כל", "בה"), "you shall not lack anything in it — ONE seat; 2:7\'s \'you lacked nothing\' the wilderness\'s twin; the lack-verb seven Torah seats; THE PROHIBITION FORM AS A PROMISE (the morphology: not + imperfect, second person)"), (("ארץ", "אשר", "אבניה", "ברזל"), "a land whose stones are iron — ONE seat; \'iron\' eight in the book (computed)"), (("ומהרריה", "תחצב", "נחשת"), "and from its hills you shall hew copper — the hew-verb\'s Torah seats 6:11 (the cisterns, twice) and 8:9 (computed)"))} → {AP(8, 9, (("ארעא", "די", "לא", "בעצורין", "תיכול", "בה", "לחמא"), "a land where not in STRAITS shall you eat bread — \'poverty\' made \'straits\' (one seat)"), (("לא", "תחסר", "כל", "מדעם", "בה"), "you shall not lack any thing in it — \'any thing\' the Aramaic\'s word (nine seats, computed)"), (("ומטורהא", "תפסול", "נחשא"), "and from its mountains you shall hew copper"))}. THE SHELF (37:5): the Land spiced with everything — \'you shall not lack anything\'. MATERIAL for the poverty-word\'s one seat and the shelf\'s reading.')
row(8, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'AND YOU SHALL EAT AND BE SATISFIED, AND YOU SHALL BLESS THE LORD YOUR GOD FOR THE GOOD LAND WHICH HE HAS GIVEN YOU. {HP(8, 10, (("ואכלת", "ושבעת", "וברכת"), "and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless — ONE seat; THE TORAH\'S ONE COMMAND TO BLESS THE LORD (\'and you shall bless the LORD\' one seat — computed); \'eat and be satisfied\' six in the book; the SATED VERB STARRED by the parser as the seven-stem homograph (asserted)"), (("את", "יהוה", "אלהיך", "על", "הארץ", "הטבה"), "the LORD your God for the good land — \'the good land which He has given you\' ONE (computed)"), (("אשר", "נתן", "לך"), "which He has given you — five seats in the book (computed)"))} → {AP(8, 10, (("ותיכול", "ותשבע", "ותברך", "ית", "יי", "אלהך"), "and you shall eat and be satisfied and bless the LORD your God — the bless-form one seat (computed)"), (("על", "ארעא", "טבתא", "דיהב", "לך"), "for the good land which He gave you"))}. THE SHELF (40:10): the blessing reaches even the eating and the satisfaction — this verse the rung. The compile: the blessing after the meal (Berakhot 48b — the grace\'s blessings from this verse; 20b-21a the Torah obligation; 49b the measure of \'satisfied\'). MATERIAL for the one command to bless.')

